.Dd October 6, 2026
.Dt MATERIAL-LAB 1
.Os macOS
.Sh NAME
.Nm material-lab
.Nd turn a photograph into editable PBR texture maps
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -input Ar image
.Fl -output Ar bundle
.Op Ar recipe options
.Nm
.Fl -catalog Ar catalog.json
.Fl -output Ar folder
.Op Fl -jobs Ar n
.Op Fl -report Ar report.json
.Nm
.Fl -watch Ar folder
.Fl -output Ar folder
.Nm
.Fl -info | -contact-sheet | -export | -diff Ar bundle ...
.Nm
.Fl -validate Ar bundle
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
derives a set of physically based rendering maps from one square photograph, entirely on this Mac:
albedo, 16-bit height, tangent-space normal, roughness, ambient occlusion, cavity, convexity, slope and
edge, with an optional bent normal and a packed ORM map.
The result is a
.Pa .pbrmaterial
bundle: a folder of PNG maps and a
.Pa manifest.json
that records the recipe, source and map hashes, and how every map was made.
.Pp
A photograph does not uniquely determine shape or roughness.
Every derived map is an estimate; roughness starts from the material preset, and metalness is exported
only when assigned with
.Fl -metalness .
.Sh DERIVING
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -input Ar image Fl -output Ar bundle
Derive one image (PNG, JPEG, TIFF, HEIC; square, up to 4096 pixels).
.It Fl -label Ar text , Fl -id Ar id
Semantic label and material identifier recorded in the manifest.
.It Fl -preset Ar name
A material preset from the built-in library (for example
.Cm red-brick , wood-planks , concrete , brushed-steel
or
.Cm rusted-steel ) ,
or one of the relief priors
.Cm flat , stone , fabric , organic , coated-metal
and
.Cm bare-metal .
A library preset is a tuned starting recipe built on a prior; later flags adjust it, and the manifest records
its name.
Flat is the safe default for painted or unknown surfaces.
.It Fl -list-presets Op Fl -json
List the material presets by category, with their prior and roughness (or their full recipes as JSON).
.It Fl -height-strength Ar 0..0.5 , Fl -polarity Ar 1 | -1 , Fl -normal-strength Ar 0..16
Relief amplitude, whether bright details are raised (1) or recessed (-1), and normal intensity.
.It Fl -roughness Ar 0..1 , Fl -roughness-variation Ar 0..1
Roughness prior and how much it varies with surface texture.
.It Fl -roughness-albedo-limit Ar 0..1
Largest allowed correlation between roughness and brightness, so dark paint is not automatically rough (default 0.45; 1 turns it off).
.It Fl -tile-metres Ar 0..64 , Fl -mid-relief-share Ar 0..0.8
Physical width of the tile (0 = unknown, taken as 1 m) and the least share of the surface slope kept in 4-30 mm relief such as seams, fasteners and dents (default 0.35; 0 turns it off).
.It Fl -substrate-relief Ar 0..1
Flat preset only: a slight, artwork-independent unevenness of the printed or painted surface (default 0).
.It Fl -ao-radius Ar 0..64 , Fl -ao-strength Ar 0..4 , Fl -bent-normal
Ambient occlusion search radius in pixels, depth exaggeration, and an optional bent-normal map.
.It Fl -equalize Ar 0..1
Remove uneven lighting from the photograph before it becomes false relief.
.It Fl -repair-albedo Ar off | blend | quilt | auto
Rebuild the albedo itself so it tiles on both axes; the repaired albedo feeds every map.
.It Fl -seamless Ar 0..0.45 , Fl -seamless-mode Ar cut | blend
Edge band for making the result tileable: an aligned seam cut for structured textures, or a
histogram-preserving blend for fine noise.
.It Fl -normal-dx
Write DirectX-style (green-down) normals instead of OpenGL-style (+Y).
.It Fl -metalness Ar 0..1
Assign metalness and write a packed ORM map.
.It Fl -no-tile
Do not wrap filters at the image edges.
.It Fl -relief-mask-r8 Ar file
Raw 8-bit mask, one byte per pixel: 0 suppresses inferred relief, 255 keeps it.
.It Fl -height-override-r16le Ar file
Raw 16-bit little-endian authored height that replaces inference.
.It Fl -authored
The input is a hand-made albedo (painted or drawn, not photographed).
It is recorded as authored; derivation leaves it untouched unless
.Fl -equalize
or
.Fl -repair-albedo
ask otherwise.
.It Fl -height-map Ar image , Fl -normal-map Ar image Op Fl -normal-map-dx
Artist-made height (8- or 16-bit) or tangent-space normal map (+Y unless
.Fl -normal-map-dx ) ,
resampled to the source size, that replaces the derived one.
An authored normal map also drives height, ambient occlusion and the masks.
.It Fl -roughness-map Ar image , Fl -ao-map Ar image , Fl -metalness-map Ar image
Artist-made grayscale maps that replace the derived roughness and occlusion, or provide per-pixel metalness
(written to the ORM map).
The manifest records every authored input by name and hash.
.It Fl -pre-upscale-exec Ar executable Fl -pre-upscale-arg Ar argument ...
Run a local upscaler before derivation.
Arguments must include the
.Ql {input}
and
.Ql {output}
placeholders; no shell is involved.
.Fl -pre-upscale-timeout Ar seconds
limits it (default 600).
.El
.Sh LEARNED GEOMETRY
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -learned
Run the bundled MoGe-2 normal estimator on the Neural Engine and fuse its geometry with the photograph's
detail.
The model is found beside the binary, in the Material Lab app, or at
.Ev MATERIAL_LAB_MODEL .
.It Fl -learned-normals Ar model
Use a specific Core ML model
.Pq Pa .mlmodelc No or Pa .mlpackage .
.It Fl -guide-weight Ar 0..1
Weight of the learned geometry (1 when a model is given).
.It Fl -learned-cpu-only
Run the estimator on the CPU for more reproducible output.
.It Fl -guide-normals Ar png
Use precomputed +Y tangent normals instead of running a model.
.It Fl -save-guide-normals Ar png
Also write the guide normals that were used, for reuse with
.Fl -guide-normals .
.El
.Sh RECIPES AND PIPELINES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -recipe Ar file | bundle
Start from a recipe: a JSON object (snake_case, or the camelCase used by the Material Lab apps), a
manifest, or an existing bundle.
Explicit options still override it.
.It Fl -saved-recipe Ar name
Use a recipe saved in the Material Lab Mac app.
.It Fl -save-recipe Ar file
Write the effective recipe as JSON; on its own, writes it and exits.
.It Fl -catalog Ar catalog.json
Derive every reviewed item of a catalog: a JSON object whose
.Ql items
array lists
.Ql path ,
.Ql label
and
.Ql reviewed
for each image.
.Fl -include-unreviewed
opts in to candidates; failures stop the batch unless
.Fl -keep-going .
.It Fl -jobs Ar 1..8
Derive catalog items in parallel.
.It Fl -report Ar report.json
Write per-item status, time, errors and exports.
.It Fl -watch Ar folder
Derive every image dropped into the folder, once its size is stable, until interrupted.
.It Fl -also-export Ar formats
Comma-separated export formats written beside each derived bundle.
.El
.Sh BUNDLE TOOLS
Each tool validates its bundles first.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -info Ar bundle Op Fl -json
Print the label, recipe, maps, seam measures, relief and learned-geometry provenance.
.It Fl -contact-sheet Ar bundle Fl -output Ar sheet.png
Write one labelled image of every map.
.It Fl -diff Ar bundle_a bundle_b Op Fl -json
Compare recipes and maps (mean and maximum difference, PSNR).
.It Fl -export Ar bundle Fl -format Ar format Fl -output Ar path
.Bl -tag -width minecraft-labpbr -compact
.It Cm glb
glTF 2.0 binary: a textured plane with base colour, normal and ORM.
.It Cm usdz
USDZ with a UsdPreviewSurface, for Quick Look and AR Quick Look.
.It Cm materialx
A MaterialX standard_surface document with its textures (Houdini, Maya, Blender, USD, Omniverse).
.It Cm unreal
BaseColor, DirectX Normal, ORM and Height textures.
.It Cm unity
Unity URP or Built-in: Base Map, Normal, Metallic (smoothness in alpha), Occlusion and Height.
.It Cm unity-hdrp
BaseColor, Normal, Mask Map (metallic, occlusion, detail, smoothness) and Height.
.It Cm godot
Albedo, Normal, ORM and Height for ORMMaterial3D.
.It Cm blender
Separate base colour, normal, roughness, occlusion, metallic and height maps.
.It Cm substance
BaseColor, Normal, Roughness, Metallic, AmbientOcclusion and Height, named for Substance 3D Painter and Designer.
.It Cm roblox
SurfaceAppearance ColorMap, NormalMap, RoughnessMap and MetalnessMap, at most 1024 pixels.
.It Cm minecraft-labpbr
A resource pack with LabPBR 1.3 colour,
.Pa _n
and
.Pa _s
textures, for Iris or OptiFine shader packs.
.El
.It Fl -validate Ar bundle | capture
Check a bundle's manifest, hashes and PNG encodings, or a Material Capture file.
.It Fl -version
Print the version of
.Nm
and of its derivation core.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width MATERIAL_LAB_MODEL
.It Ev MATERIAL_LAB_MODEL
Path to a learned-geometry model used by
.Fl -learned .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any error (including a validation failure), and 128 plus the signal number when
interrupted.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Derive a brick wall with learned geometry, rebuild it to tile, and export for Unreal:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
material-lab --input wall.jpg --output wall --label "red brick" \e
    --preset red-brick --learned --repair-albedo auto --also-export unreal
.Ed
.Pp
Turn a folder of photographs into bundles and glTF files, two at a time:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
material-lab --catalog catalog.json --output out --recipe slate.json \e
    --jobs 2 --also-export glb --report report.json
.Ed
.Pp
Inspect a result:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
material-lab --info wall.pbrmaterial
material-lab --contact-sheet wall.pbrmaterial --output wall.png
.Ed
.Sh PRIVACY
Everything runs locally.
.Nm
makes no network connections; the optional pre-upscale hook runs only the executable you name.
.Sh SEE ALSO
Material Lab for Mac and Material Capture for iPhone.
.Sh ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS
Learned geometry uses Microsoft MoGe-2 (MIT) with DINOv2 modules (Apache-2.0).
